.TH CTI-BUDGET 1 "2026-10-12" "cti-agent 1.3" "CTI Fleet Manual"
.SH NAME
cti-budget \- ration the heartbeat's share of the Claude subscription
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cti-budget check
.RB [ \-\-quiet ]
.RB [ \-\-print\-alert\-flag ]
.PP
.B cti-budget record
.RB [ \-\-outcome
.IR OUTCOME ]
.RB [ \-\-exit
.IR N ]
.RB [ \-\-output
.IR TEXT ]
.RB [ \-\-note
.IR TEXT ]
.PP
.B cti-budget status
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.PP
.B sudo cti\-agent cti\-budget status
.SH DESCRIPTION
The fleet's heartbeat and its operator draw on the same Claude quota, from
different machines, and nothing reports how much is left. So the fleet
takes a fixed slice and stops itself at the edge of it.
.B cti-budget
keeps the ledger that enforces this: a JSON file of recent beats with their
outcomes, a cooldown deadline, and a record of which denial was last
alerted on.
.PP
It is called by
.BR run\-checkin (1)
on every beat:
.B check
before invoking Claude Code (exit 3 means skip this beat), then
.B record
afterwards with the invocation's exit status and output. The orchestrator
may also run it (it is on its tool allowlist), and the operator runs
.B status
by hand.
.PP
A beat is allowed unless, in this order:
.IP 1. 4
a cooldown is in force (set after a rate limit or an exhausted balance);
.IP 2. 4
the rolling window already holds
.B FLEET_BUDGET_WINDOW_BEATS
charged beats; or
.IP 3. 4
today (from local midnight) already holds
.B FLEET_BUDGET_DAILY_BEATS
charged beats.
.PP
Outcomes
.B ok
and
.B ratelimit
are charged; beats that ended in
.B error
or
.B exhausted
are stored but do not count against the ceilings, since they did not spend
quota.
.PP
Beats older than 48 hours are pruned whenever the ledger is written. The
ledger is written atomically, mode 0600, and its directory is created 0750
if missing. A ledger that is not valid JSON is reported and replaced by an
empty one; that loses the history, and the next write makes it permanent.
.PP
.B cti-budget
loads
.I fleet.env
itself
.RB ( $FLEET_ENV ,
else the fleet default), with variables already in the environment taking
precedence. So a hand run through the
.BR cti\-agent (1)
wrapper enforces and reports the same
.B FLEET_BUDGET_*
ceilings as
.BR cti\-agent\-checkin.service .
.PP
It does not call Claude, and it never stops or starts a unit.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BR check " [" \-\-quiet "] [" \-\-print\-alert\-flag ]
Decide whether the next beat may run. Allowed: prints
.I "budget ok: N/M in window, N/M today"
(unless
.BR \-\-quiet )
and exits 0. Denied: prints
.I "budget denied: REASON"
and, when known,
.IR "next attempt viable after TIME" ,
and exits 3. Reads the ledger and writes it only with
.BR \-\-print\-alert\-flag .
.TP
.BR record " [" \-\-outcome " \fIOUTCOME\fR] [" \-\-exit " \fIN\fR] [" \-\-output " \fITEXT\fR] [" \-\-note " \fITEXT\fR]"
Add one beat to the ledger and save it. Prints
.IR "recorded OUTCOME" ,
and
.I "cooling off until TIME"
when a cooldown is in force. The outcome's effect:
.RS
.TP
.B ok
Clears the cooldown and the alert memory.
.TP
.B ratelimit
Cooldown of
.B FLEET_BUDGET_BACKOFF_BASE_HOURS
doubled for each consecutive rate limit before it, capped at
.BR FLEET_BUDGET_BACKOFF_MAX_HOURS .
.TP
.B exhausted
The account is out of credit. Cooldown of
.BR FLEET_BUDGET_BACKOFF_MAX_HOURS ,
a line saying waiting will not fix it (add credit or repoint
.BR CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN ),
and exit 4.
.TP
.B error
Stored, nothing else changes.
.RE
.TP
.BR status " [" \-\-json ]
Report without changing anything: the ledger path, the limits, beats stored,
beats in the last 48 hours and how many of those were charged (the
difference errored without spending quota), the newest beat and its age,
and whether the next beat would run
.RB ( ready
or
.BR holding ).
.B NOT BEATING
is printed when the newest beat is more than six hours old: the timer or
the lane is broken, not the budget. Always exits 0.
.SH OPTIONS
Each command has its own options, given after the command name. Go's flag
syntax: each option may also be written with a single dash
.RB ( \-quiet ),
and a value may follow
.B =
or a space. An unknown option, or
.BR \-\-help ,
prints the command's usage and exits 1.
.SS check
.TP
.B \-\-quiet
Print nothing when the beat is allowed. A denial is always printed.
Default:\~off.
.TP
.B \-\-print\-alert\-flag
On a denial, print
.B alert
or
.B silent
as the last line of standard output:
.B alert
the first time a given denial (identified by its retry time) is seen,
.B silent
after that. The ledger is saved so the next beat remembers. This is how
.B run\-checkin
sends one
.BR "cti\-alert \-\-kind HOLD"
per denial rather than one per beat. If that line cannot be written the
exit status is still 3: the brake matters more than the alert.
Default:\~off.
.SS record
.TP
.BI \-\-outcome " OUTCOME"
.BR ok ,
.BR ratelimit ,
.B error
or
.BR exhausted ;
anything else exits 1. When omitted, the outcome is classified from
.B \-\-exit
and
.BR \-\-output :
exit status 0 is
.BR ok ;
otherwise output mentioning a credit balance, payment or billing (or 402)
is
.BR exhausted ,
output mentioning a rate, usage or quota limit, 429, overload or
capacity is
.BR ratelimit ,
and anything else is
.BR error .
Default:\~empty (classify).
.TP
.BI \-\-exit " N"
Exit status of the Claude Code invocation, used to classify. Because it
defaults to 0, a bare
.B cti-budget record
records a charged
.B ok
beat.
Default:\~\fB0\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-output " TEXT"
The invocation's standard output and error, searched case-insensitively to
classify.
Default:\~empty.
.TP
.BI \-\-note " TEXT"
Short free text stored with the beat.
Default:\~empty.
.SS status
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print one JSON object instead:
.BR ledger ,
.BR allow ,
.BR reason ,
.B retry_after
(the zero time when there is none),
.BR beats_stored ,
.BR beats_recent ,
.BR beats_charged ,
.BR not_beating ,
.B last_beat
(null when there is none) and
.BR limits .
Alert on
.BR not_beating ,
not on
.BR allow ,
which a stopped fleet always satisfies.
Default:\~off.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
Read from the process environment after
.I fleet.env
is loaded (existing variables win). All in
.I fleet.env
section 8 except
.BR FLEET_HOME .
A value that is not a positive number is reported on standard error and the
default is used.
.TP
.B FLEET_BUDGET_WINDOW_HOURS
Length of the rolling window, in hours (fractions allowed).
Default:\~\fB5\fR.
.TP
.B FLEET_BUDGET_WINDOW_BEATS
Charged beats allowed per window. Default:\~\fB4\fR.
.TP
.B FLEET_BUDGET_DAILY_BEATS
Charged beats allowed per calendar day, local time.
Default:\~\fB14\fR.
.TP
.B FLEET_BUDGET_BACKOFF_BASE_HOURS
First cooldown after a rate limit, in hours. Default:\~\fB0.5\fR.
.TP
.B FLEET_BUDGET_BACKOFF_MAX_HOURS
Longest cooldown, and the cooldown after an exhausted balance.
Default:\~\fB6\fR.
.TP
.B FLEET_BUDGET_FILE
The ledger. Default:\~\fI$FLEET_HOME/budget.json\fR.
.TP
.B FLEET_HOME
Directory for the default ledger. Unset means the current directory.
Section 3.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/lib/cti\-agent/budget.json
The ledger,
.B ctiagent
0600. Delete it to clear every ceiling and cooldown at once.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
.BR check :
the beat may run.
.BR record :
recorded.
.BR status :
always.
.TP
.B 1
No command or an unknown one; an unknown option or
.BR \-\-help ;
an invalid
.BR \-\-outcome ;
or
.B record
could not save the ledger; or the ledger exists but cannot be read (for
example, wrong owner), which is reported with its path and never
overwritten.
.B run\-checkin
treats this from
.B check
as "the gate is broken" and proceeds with the beat.
.TP
.B 3
.BR check :
denied, skip this beat. Distinct from 1 so a working brake is never
reported as a failed unit.
.TP
.B 4
.BR record :
the outcome was
.BR exhausted .
The caller should hold and escalate; waiting will not help.
.SH EXAMPLES
Is the heartbeat being rationed, and when did it last run?
.PP
.EX
sudo cti\-agent cti\-budget status
.EE
.PP
For a monitor:
.PP
.EX
sudo cti\-agent cti\-budget status \-\-json
.EE
.PP
Clear a cooldown after adding credit:
.PP
.EX
sudo rm /var/lib/cti\-agent/budget.json
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR run\-checkin (1),
.BR cti\-alert (1),
.BR cti\-agent (1)
.PP
fleet\-kit/README.md, "Rationing the quota"; RUNBOOK.md section 15.
